                    {
                        "translation_id": "31adb927-c383-4c8e-b8b3-2fe1d24f5e59",
                        "source_entry_id": "f790d78a-ba27-38fc-9d18-d5b1638b6d8f",
                        "source_sense_id": "345d3bd2-49d3-311c-8b41-8aaf32f9675b",
                        "source_sense_description": "Иноязычные аналоги",
                        "target_lang_word": "Abraham",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Abraham",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bc486d7e-3060-3889-947a-9c89b32ae358",
                                        "entry_id": "fd519009-069e-3efc-9a8f-63cf354d4aeb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A prophet in the Old Testament, Qur'an and Aqdas; a Semitic patriarch son of Terah who practiced monotheism, father of the Jewish patriarch Isaac by Sarah and the Arab patriarch Ishmael by Hagar."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85db6d5c-c262-424c-b135-008fb951cefb",
                                                "sense_id": "bc486d7e-3060-3889-947a-9c89b32ae358",
                                                "text": "Neither ſhall thy name any more be called Abram, but thy name ſhall bee Abraham: for a father of many nations haue I made thee."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd5cfa15-f8fb-4b9f-8bff-df751813c946",
                                                "sense_id": "bc486d7e-3060-3889-947a-9c89b32ae358",
                                                "text": "As one would expect of caravan people around 1900 B.C., the caravan people depicted in the Khnum-hotpe grave had donkeys, whereas the Bible says that Abraham and his people, who according to the traditional interpretation are supposed to have lived at the same period, already possessed camels."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "23177112-dd89-3221-b38e-be26e5128e26",
                                        "entry_id": "fd519009-069e-3efc-9a8f-63cf354d4aeb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A male given name from Hebrew."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a87844e-a343-4f59-9710-0bec03a7ba9a",
                                                "sense_id": "23177112-dd89-3221-b38e-be26e5128e26",
                                                "text": "\"Lincoln wasn't a Jew, was he?\" he said. \"I'm sure not,\" I said. […] \"The name Abraham is very suspicious, to say the least,\" said Goebbels. \"I'm sure his parents didn't realize that it was a Jewish name,\" I said. \"They must have just liked the sound of it. They were simple frontier people. If they'd known the name was Jewish, I'm sure they would have called him something more American, like George or Stanley or Fred.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cd0a102f-820b-3855-a38e-2ad7841198cd",
                                        "entry_id": "fd519009-069e-3efc-9a8f-63cf354d4aeb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A surname originating as a patronymic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14c70056-51d9-4366-87d2-e2c538fe00e5",
                                                "sense_id": "cd0a102f-820b-3855-a38e-2ad7841198cd",
                                                "text": "Farmer also happened to be just the kind of expert that Franck and his co-author Daniel Abraham needed to bring their novels to the screen."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4a54ed6c-c5bd-3ff6-bc69-858c5e18ceda",
                                        "entry_id": "fd519009-069e-3efc-9a8f-63cf354d4aeb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The 14th sura (chapter) of the Qur'an."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
